before anybody wakes up,

00:32:06.440 --> 00:32:08.610
and like you're doing a great job at that.

00:32:08.610 --> 00:32:10.610
That should be making a
difference the rest of your day.

00:32:10.610 --> 00:32:12.980
Even the good parts of what I'm doing,

00:32:12.980 --> 00:32:15.210
I turn into a critique of myself,

00:32:15.210 --> 00:32:18.590
and I, you know, I don't know.

00:32:18.590 --> 00:32:20.896
That's just what I'm
processing at this point, but.

00:32:20.896 --> 00:32:22.894
Well, interestingly,

00:32:22.894 --> 00:32:26.420
you're a one, which is a perfectionist,

00:32:26.420 --> 00:32:30.350
and I'm a three, which is
like a performer/achiever,

00:32:30.350 --> 00:32:33.853
and I mean all the Innergram numbers,

00:32:35.180 --> 00:32:37.740
and again, we will do
an Innergram episode.

00:32:37.740 --> 00:32:39.770
We say we would, but the
reason we haven't done it yet

00:32:39.770 --> 00:32:41.890
is because I just don't like

00:32:41.890 --> 00:32:43.700
to speak out of school about things,

00:32:43.700 --> 00:32:46.610
and I don't feel like
I've read enough about it,

00:32:46.610 --> 00:32:49.610
but anyway, the.

00:32:49.610 --> 00:32:50.940
You can't perform it well enough?

00:32:50.940 --> 00:32:52.080
Yeah, exactly,

00:32:52.080 --> 00:32:55.360
But one of the interesting
things about both ones and threes

00:32:55.360 --> 00:32:59.100
is that they're both deeply
self-critical, right,

00:32:59.100 --> 00:33:00.413
for different reasons.

00:33:03.040 --> 00:33:05.600
It's actually very, it's different,

00:33:05.600 --> 00:33:08.060
but there's a similarity to it

00:33:08.060 --> 00:33:10.030
because it has to do
with your performance.

00:33:10.030 --> 00:33:15.030
Like a one is critical
of how you're performing,

00:33:16.630 --> 00:33:20.300
but a three is very critical
of how they're performing

00:33:20.300 --> 00:33:23.770
as well, and so I definitely feel that.

00:33:23.770 --> 00:33:26.470
I feel we probably
experience it differently,

00:33:26.470 --> 00:33:27.740
but I feel this is the same thing.

00:33:27.740 --> 00:33:30.380
It's just like I'm always.

00:33:30.380 --> 00:33:32.850
You might be thinking
am I doing this right,

00:33:32.850 --> 00:33:34.833
and I'm thinking am I doing enough?

00:33:35.720 --> 00:33:39.480
Like that's, I tend to just think about

00:33:39.480 --> 00:33:41.240
man, I don't want this
time to have gone by

00:33:41.240 --> 00:33:43.323
and I don't have anything to show for it.

00:33:44.420 --> 00:33:47.950
Because my tendency as a
three is to find my self-worth

00:33:47.950 --> 00:33:49.330
in the things that I accomplish.

00:33:49.330 --> 00:33:53.093
So if I look at this time,
this downtime that we had,

00:33:53.093 --> 00:33:55.820
it's like, oh, this is an opportunity.

00:33:55.820 --> 00:33:58.420
This is an opportunity
to get stuff figured out,

00:33:58.420 --> 00:34:00.690
to get yourself figured out,

00:34:00.690 --> 00:34:02.760
to get your business figured out,

00:34:02.760 --> 00:34:04.920
to figure out what your
strategies are gonna be,

00:34:04.920 --> 00:34:07.870
and to know what you're
going to accomplish,

00:34:07.870 --> 00:34:09.990
figuring out what you're
going to accomplish,

00:34:09.990 --> 00:34:13.300
and I think that there
is good in that, right?

00:34:13.300 --> 00:34:16.650
I mean I think this is one of the reasons

00:34:16.650 --> 00:34:18.740
that we've done a lot of
the things that we've done

00:34:18.740 --> 00:34:21.926
is because of the way that
our personalities mix,

00:34:21.926 --> 00:34:26.101
but both of us are kind of
driving towards accomplishing.

00:34:26.101 --> 00:34:28.778
I'm kind of driving
towards accomplishing more,

00:34:28.778 --> 00:34:32.680
and you're driving towards
accomplishing things better.

00:34:32.680 --> 00:34:34.038
You know?
Yeah.

00:34:34.038 --> 00:34:35.233
And I think that those two things,

00:34:35.233 --> 00:34:38.178
that one-three combination is a big key

00:34:38.178 --> 00:34:40.200
to a lot of things that
have happened for us,

00:34:40.200 --> 00:34:42.370
but it also can be, you know,

00:34:42.370 --> 00:34:44.080
your greatest strength is
your greatest weakness,

00:34:44.080 --> 00:34:45.192
it can be our downfall.

00:34:45.192 --> 00:34:47.570
One thing that was really
helpful to me the other day,

00:34:47.570 --> 00:34:49.240
speaking of meditation, was,

00:34:49.240 --> 00:34:51.473
in the guided meditation that I was doing,

00:34:52.329 --> 00:34:55.890
talking about kindness
and kindness to yourself,

00:34:55.890 --> 00:34:59.723
I think incidentally this
is something that growing up

00:34:59.723 --> 00:35:04.320
evangelical was a really
difficult thing for both of us.

00:35:04.320 --> 00:35:08.671
I think that we've always heard
the term sort of self-care

00:35:08.671 --> 00:35:13.290
and self kindness as
an inherently prideful

00:35:13.290 --> 00:35:18.290
and selfish thing because everything

00:35:18.380 --> 00:35:20.910
had to be about others first,

00:35:20.910 --> 00:35:23.210
and I actually think that
if you really want others

00:35:23.210 --> 00:35:25.837
to be first, then you gotta make sure

00:35:25.837 --> 00:35:29.570
that you're kind to yourself
and you're loving yourself,

00:35:29.570 --> 00:35:33.063
not in this, you know,

00:35:33.930 --> 00:35:36.700
self, the whole the thing
that we began to learn

00:35:36.700 --> 00:35:38.650
in the 80s and 90s which was all about

00:35:38.650 --> 00:35:41.110
everybody's special and everybody,

00:35:41.110 --> 00:35:41.970
all about your self-image.

00:35:41.970 --> 00:35:44.210
I'm not talking about
that, but I'm just saying

00:35:44.210 --> 00:35:45.690
being kind to yourself,

00:35:45.690 --> 00:35:49.600
like one thing that struck
me in that meditation

00:35:49.600 --> 00:35:54.600
was treat yourself the way
that you would treat others,

00:35:56.580 --> 00:35:59.040
which what we hear a lot of
times which is the golden rule,

00:35:59.040 --> 00:36:00.810
we treat others the way that
you would treat yourself,

00:36:00.810 --> 00:36:03.530
which is an incredible thing
we should all live by it,

00:36:03.530 --> 00:36:05.390
but there's a different
way to see that sometimes

00:36:05.390 --> 00:36:09.690
which is I tend to be very
gracious towards people.

00:36:09.690 --> 00:36:11.180
Like when when I hear you talking

00:36:11.180 --> 00:36:13.530
about being hard on yourself

00:36:13.530 --> 00:36:18.330
for not feeling like
you're doing things right,

00:36:18.330 --> 00:36:20.200
I'm like, oh, come on, man,
don't be so hard on yourself.

00:36:20.200 --> 00:36:21.680
Like my natural inclination,

00:36:21.680 --> 00:36:23.870
and I think most of the
people listening will be to,

00:36:23.870 --> 00:36:25.600
hey, give yourself a break,

00:36:25.600 --> 00:36:27.530
but sometimes it's very
difficult to direct

00:36:27.530 --> 00:36:30.500
that type of grace back on yourself.

00:36:30.500 --> 00:36:35.500
So for me it was like just
know that you're okay.

00:36:35.580 --> 00:36:36.883
You're accepted.

00:36:38.170 --> 00:36:41.620
You're not going to increase

00:36:43.420 --> 00:36:45.610
the love that is available for you

00:36:45.610 --> 00:36:46.850
